  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol. \n1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ . \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 37.689 + 0.032 \\times 10^{-3} T - 2.156 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=37.689\\times10^{-3}T+0.016\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+2.156\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-11.962$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -10.114 + 4.823 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 5.152 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 199.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = -10.114 - 4.823 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 5.152 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 99.775 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 40.163 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -24.128 - 4.825 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.464 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 113.150 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -24.128 + 4.825 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.464 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 56.575 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 5.714 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data based on Prusaczyk (101) who estimated molecular constants. ",
    "lines_raw": [
